{"kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"1012.0963","version":"1","local":"lemma-1","file":"","label":"222ab","number":"2.1","section":"sec-2","order":1,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"(\\cite{Hagos}). \\label{222ab}\r\nA graph $G$ has exactly two main eigenvalues if and only if $G$ is\r\n2-walk $(a,b)$-linear.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","labels":["222ab"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"mainnew420zhong11.tex","from":138,"to":141},"hash":"sha256:7736428b14ff1961dbef7ed9663bbef67ea701be4c8f86e798f7f855c9779a64","minhash":"","census":"1012.0963v1#env-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.6"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"1012.0963","version":"1","local":"lemma-2","file":"","label":"21","number":"2.2","section":"sec-2","order":2,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"(\\cite{YHou}). \\label{21} Let $G$ be a 2-walk\r\n(a,b)-linear graph. Then both $a$ and $b$ are integers.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","labels":["21"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"mainnew420zhong11.tex","from":143,"to":145},"hash":"sha256:43bfed8863d40ac27b9a6b0862cb58a9deb68648cb337628efb0f8e8e9c2fb62","minhash":"","census":"1012.0963v1#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.6"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"1012.0963","version":"1","local":"lemma-3","file":"","label":"22","number":"2.3","section":"sec-2","order":3,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"(\\cite{Hu})\\label{22}. Let $G$ be a 2-walk\r\n$(a,b)$-linear graph and $v,u$ be two vertices of $G$ with unequal\r\ndegree $d(v),d(u)$, respectively. Then\r\n\\begin{equation} \\label{suv}\r\na=\\frac{S(v)-S(u)}{d(v)-d(u)}, \\\r\nb=\\frac{d(u)S(v)-d(v)S(u)}{d(v)-d(u)}.\r\n\\end{equation}","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","labels":["22","suv"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"mainnew420zhong11.tex","from":147,"to":154},"hash":"sha256:9df30b6ca68144d95bfeba30140eee11150aeb9f4b542d226a9f58451dae0452","minhash":"","census":"1012.0963v1#env-3","extractor":"ax/v0.5.6"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"1012.0963","version":"1","local":"lemma-4","file":"","label":"31","number":"2.4","section":"sec-2","order":4,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{31}\r\nLet $G\\in {\\mathcal G}$ and  $R=x_1x_2\\dots x_t$ be an internal path\r\nof length at least $2$ in $G$. Then $l(R)\\leq3$. In particular, if $\r\nl(R)=3$, then there exists no  path $Q=y_1y_2y_3$ in $G$ such that\r\n$d(y_1)=d(y_3)=d(x_1)$ and $d(y_2)=2$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","labels":["31"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"mainnew420zhong11.tex","from":164,"to":169},"hash":"sha256:3677d8d17b2b7118321cc013465677735b7d0a2c7dd6fb5c1b3e08288537ed1d","minhash":"","census":"1012.0963v1#env-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.6"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"1012.0963","version":"1","local":"lemma-5","file":"","label":"3no","number":"2.5","section":"sec-2","order":5,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{3no}\r\nLet $G\\in{\\mathcal G}$ and $v\\in V(G_{0})$.  Then\r\n\r\n(i) $G_0\\in {\\mathcal T}_i,i=1,\\dots,8$ (see Fig.~1);\r\n\r\n(ii)  $d(v)=d_{G_0}(v)$ or $a+b$;\r\n\r\n(iii) if $G$ has at least one pendent vertex, then $S(x)=a+b\\geq3$\r\nand\r\n $a\\geq2$;\r\n\r\n(iv) for a cycle $C=x_1x_2\\dots x_tx_1$ of $G$ with\r\n$d_{G_0}(x_1)\\geq 3$, $d_{G_0}(x_2)=2$, if $G$ has at least one\r\npendent vertex, then there is an integer $i\\in\\{1,2,\\dots,t\\}$ such\r\nthat $d(x_i)\\neq a+b$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","labels":["3no"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"mainnew420zhong11.tex","from":171,"to":186},"hash":"sha256:c4443edf2f82142d1ccf4d07f07b2851c7945d33bb39d913eb1f8bde8c351554","minhash":"","census":"1012.0963v1#env-5","extractor":"ax/v0.5.6"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"1012.0963","version":"1","local":"lemma-6","file":"","label":"p","number":"3.1","section":"sec-3","order":6,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{p}\r\nLet $G\\in{\\mathcal G}$ has at least one pendent vertex and let\r\n$R=x_1x_2\\dots x_t$ be an internal path or an internal cycle of\r\nlength at least $3$ in $G_0$ with $d_{G_0}(x_1)=d_{G_0}(x_t)\\in\r\n\\{3,4,6\\}$ or $d_{G_0}(x_1)=3,d_{G_0}(x_t)=5$. Then\r\n\r\n(i) $ d(x_2)= d(x_3)=\\dots=d(x_{t-1})\\in\\{2,a+b\\}$ and\r\n$d(x_1)=d(x_t)$;\r\n\r\n(ii) if $d(x_2)=2$, then $l(R)=3$;\r\n\r\n(iii) if $R$ is a cycle with $ d_{G_0}(x_1)\\in\\{3,4,6\\}$, then\r\n$l(R)=3$ and $d(x_2)=d(x_3)=2$. In particular, if $d_{G_0}(x_1)=3$,\r\nthen $a=2$;\r\n\r\n(iv) if $R$ is a cycle with $ d_{G_0}(x_1)=5$, then $l(R)=3$,\r\n$d(x_2)=d(x_3)\\in\\{2,3\\}$. In particular, if $d(x_2)=d(x_3)=3$, then\r\n$ d(x_1)=5 $ and $a=3,b=0$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","labels":["p"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"mainnew420zhong11.tex","from":194,"to":212},"hash":"sha256:ff7ea19237df34e512283b04aa578df92042fe6357748eb106d7ea03ec526334","minhash":"","census":"1012.0963v1#env-6","extractor":"ax/v0.5.6"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"1012.0963","version":"1","local":"lemma-7","file":"","label":"t1","number":"3.2","section":"sec-3","order":7,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{t1} Let $G\\in{\\mathcal\r\nG}$ with $G_0\\in {\\mathcal T}_1$ (see Fig.~1). Then $G=H_i$ for\r\n$i=1,2$ (see Fig.~3).","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","labels":["t1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"mainnew420zhong11.tex","from":297,"to":300},"hash":"sha256:faa901a8a2100eddeab88ea897bd6cfd26fecd3c1afd46af629e3020da7af4e0","minhash":"","census":"1012.0963v1#env-7","extractor":"ax/v0.5.6"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"1012.0963","version":"1","local":"lemma-8","file":"","label":"t2","number":"3.3","section":"sec-3","order":8,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{t2} Let $G\\in{\\mathcal\r\nG}$ with $G_0\\in {\\mathcal T}_2$ (see Fig.~1). Then $G=H_i$ for\r\n$i=3,4,5,6$ (see Fig.~3) or $G\\in{\\mathcal G}_j$ for $j=1,2$ (see\r\nFig.~4).","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lemma","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","labels":["t2"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"mainnew420zhong11.tex","from":378,"to":382},"hash":"sha256:19f58315ba71ced9f97ffa28e934191ff908179cb73fb0bb1575365e11f282c4","minhash":"","census":"1012.0963v1#env-8","extractor":"ax/v0.5.6"}
